      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our beds",
        "heading": "Why they are named after fells and dales.",
        "body": "<p>Borrowdale, Coniston, Grasmere, Windermere. The range takes its names from the places the walking gets done at weekends, which is also where most of the thinking about these beds happened.</p><p>Each one is built around a sleeping style rather than a price point. Curlers get walls. Sprawlers get surface. Old joints get foam that does not bottom out. Where a bed is fibre-filled rather than foam, the product page says so.</p>",
