    "pl_faq": {
      "type": "pl-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know which size to get?",
            "answer": "<p>Measure nose to base of tail while they are lying down, then add 15–20cm. Where a dog falls between two sizes, go up: sprawlers need the length more than you would think. Our <a href='/pages/size-guide'>size and firmness guide</a> has the breed-by-breed detail, and if you still get it wrong the 100-night trial covers it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does 50kg/m³ actually mean?",
            "answer": "<p>It is how much foam is packed into every cubic metre. Density and firmness are not the same thing — a low-density foam can feel firm on day one and still collapse by month six. High-density foam keeps its structure under repeated weight, which is why a 50kg/m³ core is still supporting hips and elbows years later, and why we can put a 5-year guarantee on it. You will find this core in the orthopaedic beds; the fibre-filled nest beds are built for softness instead, and each product page says which is which.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it help a dog with arthritis or hip problems?",
            "answer": "<p>These beds distribute weight so pressure is not concentrated on hips, elbows and shoulders, which is what makes lying down and getting back up harder for a dog with joint wear. A bed is not a treatment and it will not replace veterinary care, so please keep talking to your vet. What it can change is the surface they spend fourteen hours a day on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I actually wash it?",
            "answer": "<p>On most of the range, yes — properly, not just spot-clean. Covers zip off and go straight in the machine at 30°C, and on the orthopaedic beds a waterproof inner liner keeps wet coats, muddy paws and accidents away from the foam.</p><p>One exception worth knowing before you buy: our waterproof-fabric beds are wiped clean rather than washed with detergent, because detergent strips the coating off the fabric. Every product page states which applies to that bed.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How quickly will it arrive?",
            "answer": "<p>Orders are dispatched on working days and tracked from the moment they leave us. Delivery is free on UK orders over £40, and you will get tracking by email as soon as the bed is on its way.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if my dog just will not use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Then it goes back and you are not out of pocket. Let your dog sleep on it for up to 100 nights. If it is not the bed for them, contact us inside that window and we will arrange the return and refund every penny. Full terms are in our <a href='/policies/refund-policy'>returns policy</a>.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q1",
        "q2",
        "q3",
        "q4",
        "q5",
        "q6"
      ],
